A||||3||Jerry||88 GT stalls after driving - heat related?
Z||000000||Jerry||07-04-99||04:34 PM||||After driving for about an hour (might happen sooner) and slowing to a stop, the car runs rough and stalls.  It starts right away with no problem.  However, as soon as I put it in gear, it stalls again.  Currently happens about 4 or 5 times and then runs okay. Haven't had any problem around town but then again - don't need to drive far (or long) around town.  Help appreciated!!!
Z||000001||Lynx||07-05-99||01:52 AM||||Thats a WAY easy one. First you have a automatic right. If you do its the transmission not the engine (yes it sounds funny). The transmission has a TCC silenoid that goes out in those transmissions. I think its TCC orge can correct me later. Well after you buy the part all you need is a side cover gasket on the trans and you can fix it with no pulling just go through the wheel wall. My mom had the same prob with her Grand am. (Grand am uses same trans). If you look way down the list Tech list that ? has been asked before.<p>Lynx
Z||000002||theogre||07-05-99||10:31 PM||||Yup, the TCC lockup solinoid is usually it. These are still available from GM. Make sure you get the most recent version of it. It's been modified a number of times. (GM used the TH125 family tranny in Many models of cars. I think they still use it in current models.)
Z||000003||Jerry||07-08-99||06:53 PM||||Changed the solenoid.  Works great.  No problem.   Thank You.....
